# Documentation Source Structure

This file is named `README` so fsdocs ignores it while it still stays next
to the documentation source it describes.

This folder is the fsdocs source tree for the ARC Data Model documentation.
Most pages are ordinary Markdown; hands-on ProcessCore examples use literate
F# scripts so snippets can be compiled and evaluated during `BuildDocs`.

## Main Areas

- `index.md` is the documentation landing page.
- `project/` contains user-facing project guides: overview, implementation
  notes, querying background, references, examples, schemas, and prior art.
- `core-implementation/` contains executable ProcessCore usage guides. The
  `.fsx` files are literate fsdocs pages and should keep setup code hidden,
  examples small, and evaluated output focused.
- `spec/` contains the normative specification. Core model pages live under
  `spec/core/`; decoration pages live under `spec/decorations/`.
- `_head.html` is injected into every generated page and is the place for small
  site-wide presentation adapters that cannot be expressed in page frontmatter.
- `output/` is generated by fsdocs and ignored by git.

## Page Metadata

fsdocs uses YAML frontmatter to build the sidebar:

```yaml
---
title: Page Title
category: Project
categoryindex: 2
index: 1
---
```

Use `category` for the sidebar group, `categoryindex` to order groups, and
`index` to order pages inside a group. Keep normative field definitions in
`spec/`; use `project/` and `core-implementation/` for didactic guides and
library usage.

## `_head.html` Customization

`_head.html` currently adds two site-wide behaviors:

- Mermaid support: code fences marked as Mermaid are converted to Mermaid
  diagram blocks before Mermaid renders them.
- Sidebar regrouping: fsdocs emits a flat list of category headers and links.
  A small DOM transform groups `ISA Decoration`, `Workflow Run Decoration`, and
  `Datamap Decoration` under a synthetic `Decorations` heading. It also moves
  `spec/decorations/overview.md` to the first item in that group and makes each
  decoration subsection collapsible. The active decoration subsection opens
  automatically on its own pages. The same transform is applied to the desktop
  sidebar and the mobile menu.

Prefer frontmatter ordering when possible. Use `_head.html` only for behavior
that fsdocs cannot express directly, and keep comments beside any custom DOM
logic so future template changes are easier to audit.

## Build Commands

```powershell
.\build.cmd BuildDocs
.\build.cmd WatchDocs
dotnet fsdocs watch
```

`BuildDocs` evaluates literate F# pages, so NuGet restore and local package
availability affect the build.
